# Repo-root .dockerignore -- added by M15.3 (question 118) so `docker build -f
# services/lockstep-ref/Dockerfile .` does not ship this whole workspace (Rust `target/` alone
# runs into the tens of GB) as build context. Only `altavista/pb/**` and
# `services/lockstep-ref/**` are actually read by that Dockerfile; everything below is excluded
# because it is either huge, irrelevant to that image, or (GMAT R2026a) explicitly off limits
# to modify -- excluding it from a build context is not a modification, but it costs nothing to
# also leave it alone entirely.
target/
# M23.4: the scratch target dir a `docker run rust:1.85-bookworm cargo build --release
# -p av-lockstep-shim --target-dir target-docker-linux` cross-build writes to (see
# services/cfs/Dockerfile's own top comment for that command) -- never referenced by any
# Dockerfile COPY (services/cfs/bin/av-lockstep-shim, a stripped copy of just the resulting
# binary, is what gets COPYed), so excluding the whole scratch dir from every build context
# costs nothing.
target-docker-linux/
.venv/
GMAT R2026a/
.git/
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
# Local bare git mirrors third_party/fetch-cfs.sh records at fetch time (question 196(c)) --
# services/cfs/Dockerfile points CFS_MIRROR_DIR at a /tmp scratch path for its own in-container
# fetch and removes it in the same RUN layer, but a host that already has this directory (from a
# developer's own prior host-side fetch) should not have it dragged into the build context either.
third_party/mirrors/
